window.EN={"1":"The free city of Tahra, with Linoan, daughter of its former lord, as its mayor,","2":"had been resisting with all its might the Empire's evil deeds, such as the child hunts.","3":"But already","4":"it lay under siege by the imperial army led by General Paulus,","5":"and recovering from this disadvantage was expected to be extremely difficult.","6":"When the Grannvale Empire invaded northern Thracia, Tahra, by not defying the Empire,","7":"had preserved its existence as a free city, but that too seemed like a candle in the wind.","8":"I don't see List...","9":"Sir. It is thought he was either killed in battle or taken prisoner.","10":"...That was an unfortunate thing.","11":"With respect, List made light of your orders, Commander. I believe it is the natural result.","12":"...No, one cannot say only that.","13":"I had no enthusiasm for this operation, and it could be said that my hesitation, as a result, cost us many officers and men.","14":"...It is my responsibility. Laugh at me, Baldack. Even this Paulus has grown old.","15":"Commander...","16":"But I will hesitate no more. I am a soldier of Friege. I must fulfill my responsibility.","17":"Baldack, you will lend me your strength?","18":"Yes, sir. Leave it to me, Commander Paulus!","19":"The main force of my 8th Corps has also arrived. Let us begin the advance at once.","20":"Mm. I will send my own corps in support as soon as it is ready.","21":"Knowing you, General, I expect no oversights, but do be very careful.","22":"Sir. On my honor, I will accomplish the capture of Tahra without fail!!","23":"Lady Linoan, it has begun at last.","24":"The Empire's all-out attack. What is Lord Leif doing?","25":"The prince is in a war council with the other commanders.","26":"I see... Is Dean with them too?","27":"My brother said war councils don't suit his nature, and went to guard the south gate...","28":"He is a willful man.","29":"When I look at Dean, I remember the tale of the dragon knight Dain that I was told as a child.","30":"Free and easy, untroubled by small things, big, and kind, and a knight of the skies second to none...","31":"H-he is not such a fine person. You misunderstand him, Lady Linoan.","32":"No. If he had not come, I feel I would have been finished.","33":"My father was killed, the lord's mansion taken, and for two years I could not even walk freely outside,","34":"and the cruel acting governor pressed me at every turn to tell him where the prince was.","35":"When I remember how horrible it was, I still cringe.","36":"The one who rescued me from that was him... Dean.","37":"After that, too, he kept protecting me from imperial assassins, and always cheerfully encouraged me when I was apt to lose heart.","38":"He laughed and denied it, but even so I thought he must be a very renowned mercenary.","39":"But to think he was Lord Arion's subordinate...","40":"His Highness was pained by Tahra's crisis, and secretly summoned my brother and ordered him to rescue you, Lady Linoan.","41":"My brother rejoiced at the depth of His Highness's trust, and deserted the army to carry out that order.","42":"To go that far... Lord Arion...","43":"He himself could not leave his country, and yet he could not leave you, his betrothed, to die either.","44":"...It appeared to me that His Highness's distress was very deep.","45":"It will be all right, Lady Linoan. Dain and Nova will not forsake your kindness.","46":"Please believe in victory and wait. Well then, I too will now go into battle!!","47":"Hey, why are you getting your things together? You planning to leave this city?","48":"Heh... That's obvious...","49":"Hey, hey, you can't do that.","50":"The folks in this city wanted you to save them, that's why they treated you so well.","51":"Everyone's going to resent you. And a woman's grudge especially is a fearsome thing.","52":"N-no, an escort came from my country... I'm a prince of a nation too, so I can't be away from my country so much...","53":"The prince of Isaach, eh? Give it a rest. You can't fool my eyes.","54":"Urk... You knew!?","55":"I'm a bard, for all that. I know what Prince Shannan looks like, at least.","56":"Well, whatever. Do as you like. Everyone values their own life.","57":"There's no obligation to share this city's fate.","58":"Then you too...?","59":"Yeah, I'm leaving the city tomorrow. After I've taken my time enjoying tonight...","60":"I see. Then I'm off. If fate allows, we'll meet again.","61":"Hold on a sec. Meeting like this is some kind of fate too. At least tell me your real name.","62":"......Shannam.","63":"So the name at least is sort of similar... So long, Prince Shannam.","64":"It is about time... McCloy, you understand, I trust.","65":"We are entering the war by virtue of our alliance with the Empire. Whatever you do, do not start anything with the imperial army.","66":"...And then, taking advantage of the exhausted Empire's opening, we occupy Tahra...","67":"Just so. It will be an important card against Bloom. With as little damage to it as possible.","68":"Understood.","69":"Father, won't attacking Tahra only benefit the Empire?","70":"The citizens hate the Empire. If we side with them now, might we not build a new relationship between our two lands...","71":"No, it's no good. Even if we join hands with Tahra, we cannot beat the Empire.","72":"Recall Melgen Valley. Even gathering nearly all the strength of north and south Thracia, we were no match for the Empire.","73":"But that was because of that Raydrik's despicable betrayal...","74":"That may be so.","75":"But as a result of that battle, we were forced into a humiliating peace.","76":"The territory of northern Thracia we had gone to such lengths to gain fell into the Empire's hands,","77":"and it would be no exaggeration to say the Empire's national strength is now ten times ours.","78":"Would you still dare to challenge them? Are you confident you can win? Many of our people will die. Is that acceptable?","79":"No... It is as you say, Father. I was rash.","80":"...Father, I have one request...","81":"What is it?","82":"Please let me help with the capture of Tahra.","83":"...It seems you have something in mind. Well, fine.","84":"If this rich city becomes Thracia's, I do not care about the method.","85":"Try doing it as you see fit!","86":"Yes. Thank you, Father!","87":"But do not drag it out too long.","88":"Otherwise I will have to commit my main force. Do not put me to that trouble.","89":"Yes, sir.","90":"At this rate many citizens will die... I must somehow persuade Linoan...","91":"Linoan! Where are you? It's me! Arion!!","92":"Lord Arion!? Why are you here?","93":"Never mind that. Have the citizens lay down their arms. Surrender now, at once.","94":"At this rate, something irreversible will happen.","95":"Why... why is that? I can hardly believe these are your words, Prince. What on earth has happened?","96":"My father is preparing to attack with a great army.","97":"!!","98":"That is not all. Loptr's warrior monks are also heading this way.","99":"If the Berg Rosen, the \"Black Rose,\" comes, the citizens will be massacred to the last one.","100":"The Berg Rosen... Ahh, the thing I feared most...","101":"Linoan, leave it to me. Thracia will occupy Tahra. The citizens will be given every protection.","102":"Naturally I will never permit anything like the child hunts. I promise I will protect you as well, Linoan.","103":"Then what will become of Lord Leif and the other knights?","104":"They will have to escape. The Empire will not forgive the prince, and my father, too, fears him.","105":"...I understand. I will trust your word, Your Highness.","106":"Mm. Thank you for deciding.","107":"However, I will go with Lord Leif.","108":"It pains me, as it feels like abandoning the citizens who fought alongside us, but I believe that is the best way for now.","109":"And I will return to Tahra without fail. With Prince Leif, having defeated the Empire...","110":"When that time comes, Prince Arion, you will promise to return Tahra to me without fail, won't you?","111":"...Destroy the Empire, hm... Very well, I promise.","112":"But is Prince Leif a man so worthy of trust?","113":"Will he, I wonder, become an enemy to Thracia, or an ally...","114":"Either way, I would like to meet him once. With Altena, too...","115":"Ooh... nice. For you, I'd even cancel a prior engagement.","116":"What? ...What are you talking about?","117":"Like I said, I'm leaving the city after tonight.","118":"I'd like to love everyone, but I've only got the one body... hey, come on, you don't just slap a guy out of nowhere.","119":"Did I say something wrong!?","120":"What are you thinking!","121":"Even the elderly and the children are working desperately to protect this city,","122":"and you're drinking from the middle of the day... Aren't you ashamed!!","123":"Hey, there's no need to cry.","124":"Okay, okay. I just have to help too, right?","125":"But I've got a weak constitution, so spare me the heavy labor, okay?","126":"I've got no business with kids. You're interrupting my nap. Go home.","127":"I've got no business with men. Hurry up and leave.","128":"Hmm... Sorry. I'm already booked up for tonight.","129":"I've got no use for a town with this much trouble! I want out of here fast!","130":"I wonder if Tahra's done for... I'd like to start over somewhere new.","131":"My old man and my mom were both killed... I've had enough of this town!","132":"I came to this town to escape the rule of the Empire and Thracia.","133":"If it's going to be ruled by the Empire or Thracia, I have no use for this town.","134":"What on earth will happen from here? I wonder if we could live more normally in another town...","135":"I can't stand this place anymore! I want to go somewhere far away...","136":"Um... where might Lord Dean be at the moment?","137":"Oh, Lord Dean. Lady Altena is waiting for you. This way...","138":"Dean, it's been a long time. I'm relieved to see you looking well.","139":"Lady Altena!? What on earth brings you here?","140":"Heehee... You're the same as ever, Dean.","141":"And after I came all this way to give you this lance.","142":"A lance? ...This is Prince Arion's Dragon Lance.","143":"Why something so important...","144":"My brother wants you to use it. He said it is the least he can do to make amends for making you a traitor.","145":"Leaving the army was my own decision. I'm glad for the thought, but I can't accept this.","146":"Dean, don't let my brother's feelings go to waste. If you still refuse, I order you as a princess of Thracia.","147":"Heh... I'm no longer a knight of Thracia, though...","148":"Understood. If it is your order, Lady Altena, it can't be helped.","149":"I will hold on to this Dragon Lance for a while.","150":"I'm glad... Dean, protect Linoan with that lance.","151":"Linoan and my brother are promised to each other...","152":"In truth my brother would surely like to protect her himself, but he can't leave the country right now...","153":"That is why I think he entrusted that lance to you.","154":"Me, in His Highness's place...?","155":"You seem to be under some misapprehension, Lady Altena, but very well.","156":"You need not worry about Lady Linoan. I will protect her even at the cost of my life!","157":"Oh, you folks are from the Liberation Army.","158":"Sorry, but could you give this book to Lady Linoan?","159":"It was entrusted to me by the late Duke. For when the time comes, he said...","160":"I see... So that is how it is...","161":"Duke Bloom... please... realize it... If it is now... there is still... gah!","162":"I am obliged... But I must take responsibility for the defeat...","163":"Interesting. Can you defeat me, I wonder.","164":"Absurd... Why has it come to this..."};
